  "note": "Supplementary evaluation for an ROC curve exhibit. The original W5.3 open-set test (openset.json) has no negative-class examples in its test set (train=0-4, test=5/6 only), so no FPR/ROC curve can be computed from it directly. This run holds back a stratified 20% slice of label-0 (Normal) rows only (random_state=42, not seen in training) as negatives; trains on the remaining 80% of label-0 plus all of labels 1-4 (the known attack types, same as the original W5.3 training set); then scores both the held-out normal rows and the original 5/6 positives with predict_proba (score = 1 - P(predicted class = Normal)). An earlier attempt used all of labels 0-4 as the negative pool, which wrongly penalised the model for correctly flagging labels 1-4 as not-normal and produced AUC < 0.5; corrected to normal-only negatives here. This is a slightly different (smaller) training set than the original W5.3 result (80% of normal rows vs 100%), so its detection-rate-at-default-threshold is reported for cross-reference only and does NOT replace the frozen W5.3 figures (single-view 59.3%, cross-layer 50.3%) already reported in Findings_Thread.md / Ch 5 material.",
